               <history>
                  <origin>
                     <origDate when-custom="13XX" notBefore="1300" notAfter="1399" calendar="#gregorian">s. xiv</origDate>
                  </origin>
                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_94">Cambridge,
                        Cambridgeshire. Franciscan convent</orgName><p>' . . . minorum Babwell''
                        (foot of fol. 1r, erased, s. xiv). Below it in the same hand is: 'Precium 8
                        s' et dixit in vita sua quod communitas'; followed by an erasure, over which
                        is written in a 15th-cent. hand: 'fratrum minorum cantebr' haberet ex eius
                        collatione de licentia rev. fratris T. Radnor ministri'. Probably the same
                        15th-c. hand writes at top of fol. 1r: 'fratris Thome Trumpyton sacre
                        theologie doctoris'. A partially erased inscription on fol. 86v (end of the
                        original volume), s. xiv, seems to read: 'de alm[ariis fratrum de] Babwell'
                        de [?dono] fratr[is? . .] de Creyk''.</p><p>The rest of the volume is
                        earlier and may not have been bound together in the middle ages: witness the
                        chain or clasp marks on fol. 87.</p><p>Thomas Trumpington STP was president
                        of the Minoresses of Denny, 1465.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Marcello Cervini (1501–1555), cardinal, his
                     no. 869. </provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Gugliemo Sirleto (1514–1585), cardinal and
                     scholar, his no. 38.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Duke Giovanni Angelo di Altempo.</provenance>
               </history>
